We are applying for all the badges: Artifact Available, Artifact Evaluated – Functional, Reusable, Artifact Reproduced

Artifact Available:
- The code, inputs and outputs are all archived and available with DOI numbers.

AE Functional:
- We provide the ability to build ORBSLAM3 with OASIS on any system through CMake dependency management.
- We provide guidance to reproduce the paper's results, on any system. (see READMEs).
- We provide a build pipeline, and a trial production script to perform experiments.
- We provide an analysis pipeline, that can analyze the outputs of the production scripts.

AE Reusable:
- We document how to use your own data or reuse the data we collected, and application of the same analysis scripts to compare.
- We provide configuration script examples to disable or modify ORBSLAM3.
- We provide guidance to incorporate augmentations or adjustments to each pipeline (see READMEs).

AE Reproduced:
- We provide the data we collected, enabling the exact reproduction the papers results.
- For complete artifact reproduction from input, we provide ORBSLAM3 with OASIS instructions. Experiments should be done on similar/matching systems (Intel i7 6950X and Nvidia Jetson AGX Orin) to produce paper results.
- Build scripts automatically download and install dependencies for Unix Based machines
- Instructions include how to utilize Docker containers to perform trials (both on Intel and Jetson)
- Production scripts automatically randomize ordering of trials, and perform each variant multiple times, to reduce impacts of confounders.
- Analysis scripts average by variant, and produce outputs that can be compared.

